# pstack in this repository

The plugin lives at `.cursor/plugins/pstack`. Read `skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md` in full, including the Principles index, before non-trivial work.

This Cloud Agent session does not register `subagent_type: "poteto-agent"`. Use `generalPurpose` and tell the child to read that skill first.

## When to use `/poteto-mode`

Use it for any task that needs rigor: a new feature, a bug with a repro, a PR to merge-ready, a multi-agent program, or work that will be reviewed later.

Do not use it for a one-line question or a pure status check.

## Routing

- New or changed behavior: Feature playbook
- Defect: Bug fix playbook (repro first)
- "Check on PR X" / comments / CI: Babysit playbook, not Cursor's built-in babysit
- Standing multi-PR program: Orchestrate playbook (coordinator never writes product code)
- One long task to a predicate: Autonomous run
- Read-only "how does X work": Investigation / `/how`

## Models

Role-to-model mapping is in `.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`. Only those Task slugs exist here. Do not pass pstack's default names (`grok-4.6-fast-xhigh`, `gpt-5.6-sol-max`, `claude-fable-5-thinking-max`); they are not valid in this environment.

## Product work

Gridiron (Hard Rock Bet / NFL / NCAAF picks) is the standing program. Coordinator chat authors briefs and drains PRs. Workers own exclusive branches under `cursor/<name>-ce57`. Never commit `ODDS_API_KEY`.
